What I implemented:

- `engine/world/origin.hpp` and `src/origin.cpp`: `WorldOrigin`, which rebases the origin to the camera past 2048 m. Subscribers receive an `OriginShift`. `rebase_local` and `rebase_matrix` rewrite float state kept across frames.
- `cell_coord_at`, `StreamingManager::update`, `tile_distance`, and `select_terrain_lods` now take `glm::dvec2` camera positions. A float camera at 1e6 m could land in the wrong cell.
- `tests/src/world_origin_tests.cpp`, six `[unit]` cases: rebase thresholds, subscriber order and delta, far-field precision, rebased matrices, a physics-style subscriber, far-camera cell boundaries, and a 20 km route with about ten rebases that checks transforms, handles, cells, and picking.
- `docs/large-world.md` and progress-log entries.

Choices I made that you may want to change:

- Rebasing never rewrites authored transforms. The origin is only an anchor for float state, so handles and pick ids are stable by construction.
- The renderer needs no rebase, since it is already camera-relative in `double`. That keeps the GPU path unchanged.
- Physics is not wired yet. The subscriber contract is proven with a test subscriber, and the real adapter belongs to US-052 and US-053.
